The record must distinguish an AI recommendation from a human decision.

The client must not be able to manufacture authoritative decision-maker identity by submitting an arbitrary name in a request body.

The server must derive the authenticated actor from a verified identity context when authentication is available. If the identity provider is not configured, consequential decision recording must fail closed or remain disabled in a clearly documented development-only mode.

Do not assume an authentication provider exists.

#### 5.8 Actions, progress, and outcomes

